From: R0xy <liluoxi.llx@alibaba-inc.com>
Subject: [PATCH] util: Preserve const for the directory separator

GCC 15 preserves the const qualifier in strrchr's return type when
compiling with C23. The input path is read-only; only the allocated
directory buffer needs a writable pointer.

Upstream: Pending
Signed-off-by: R0xy <liluoxi.llx@alibaba-inc.com>
---
 util.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/util.c b/util.c
--- a/util.c
+++ b/util.c
@@ -1155,3 +1155,4 @@ UTI_PathToDir(const char *path)
 {
-  char *dir, *slash;
+  const char *slash;
+  char *dir;
   size_t dir_len;
